WEBVTT

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:04.840
<i>Now for our next news story.</i>

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:08.000
<i>Last night a new woman living within the city</i>

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.410
<i>was diagnosed with Astral Syndrome.</i>

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:23.160
<b>Breaking News</b>

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:23.160
<b>New Patient, 17th this Month
Doctors Hurry to Analyze the Cause of this 
Mysterious, Modern Disease</b>

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.950
<i>Astral Syndrome is a mysterious, modern disease</i>

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:18.200
<i>causing people to suddenly lose consciousness
 and eventually enter a vegetative state.</i>

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:23.160
<b>Astral Syndrome Victims Increasing</b>

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.160
<i>At present, both the cause and
 means of treatment remain unclear.</i>

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:26.380
<i>According to a handful of 
professionals, this mysterious disease</i>

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
<i>is said to originate from a certain
 vocal-synthesizer application.</i>

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.060
Many are saying that the Virtuadolls developed
 by your company are the cause of this.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.050
Do you have any comment on that?

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:43.120
Well, at present we're still
 investigating these claims,

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.310
so I'll refrain from commenting
 on any specific correlation.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.660
Then let me ask you, the team leader.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.820
Is there actually a causal relationship?
 Or is there not?

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.110
You must have some idea!

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:56.680
Why are you staying silent?!

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.620
Have you offered any 
explanation to the patients

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.500
suffering from this disease, 
or their families?!

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.460
Please give us a sincere answer!

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.340
I need to go.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.460
<i>It's my fault that μ ended up this way.</i>

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.180
<i>I need to confront her again.</i>

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.190
<i>It's like hell.</i>

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:13.250
<i>The grating noise of trains...</i>

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.300
<i>The sensation of people worming around you...</i>

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.320
<i>The prickly glare of the sun...</i>

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:24.860
<i>Even the foul smell of ramen shops...</i>

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:25.430
<b>Original Iekei Ramen Yoshida Rokuya</b>

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:28.350
<i>You feel it with all five senses.</i>

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.520
<i>There's not a single pleasant memory here.</i>

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:35.730
<i>But despite that, I've returned
 to this hell, this reality.</i>

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.190
<i>We have more news on Astral Syndrome.</i>

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:08.640
<b>The Astral Syndrome Menace</b>

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.080
<i>This morning we have confirmed the death</i>

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.440
<i>of one patient who was in a coma.</i>

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:12.040
<i>The deceased's name is Yamada Daiki-san.</i>

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.420
Cute!

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.200
<i>The now deceased Yamada Daiki-san</i>

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:27.280
<i>was a user of the vocal-synthesizer
 app known as a Virtuadoll,</i>

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:31.070
<i>once again bringing the correlation
 between the two to the fore.</i>

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.960
<i>This Astral Syndrome continues to
 be a menace within our nation.</i>

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:00.760
<i>I'm being followed?</i>

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:27.370
He's gone?

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.450
Is there someone after me?

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.870
Shopping squad's back.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.670
Sorry to do this to you all day after day.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:04.720
But we're only a little bit away
 from Master Up, so let's hang in there.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.630
I know! We're all a team, right?

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.150
Yeah, that's right!

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:11.530
Who's drinking coffee?

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:13.580
Oh, Mari-chan, I'll have
 mine with extra sugar.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:16.060
Hey, you come, too.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:17.370
Too many carbs is bad for your body.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.530
Forget about him.

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.690
He seems to prefer being alone, anyway.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.900
You're right.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:27.320
Sorry.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.860
Man...

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:54.050
What are you doing here,

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.970
Shikishima Ritsu?

00:06:58.140 --> 00:06:59.980
<b>People constantly seek out the right answer. 
Yet, is being right really all that matters?</b>

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:08.860
You're alive!

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:10.320
Take that!

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:16.370
Huh?

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:22.290
Marie-chan, why are you doing this?

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:25.850
Because I wanted to see that look
 on your face, four-eyed shrimp!

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:27.280
I've been playing along

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:30.380
with your stupid friend routine
 this whole time, all for this moment!

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.560
Right, μ?!

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:33.880
Make me happy!

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:38.720
Hardships, suffering—

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:42.600
I'll take everything for 
all of you here in Mobius!

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:57.800
<i>It's a coerced parade of emotional expression!</i>

00:07:56.840 --> 00:08:01.960
I'll make everyone even happier!

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:01.040
<i>This is who I am today!</i>

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:04.430
<i>Let's hold hands together,</i>

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:05.770
This is the best!

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:07.710
<i>and wage war on each other, hah!</i>

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:07.710
Oppression and slaughter!

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:11.340
<i>It's laughable, isn't it?</i>

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:11.340
Tormenting the weak with overwhelming power!

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:14.570
<i>We're nothing but cosmic waste,</i>

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:17.440
Where's the weak little bug and Shikishima?!

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:17.440
<i>tiny specks dancing around,</i>

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:20.240
<i>fluttering about like dust.</i>

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:20.360
I was saving the look of despair on that

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:24.040
<i>Now shatter! Until you go out and vanish,</i>

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:22.980
lame virgin bastard's face for dessert!

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:24.310
Naruko!

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:27.050
<i>come on, we can fight!</i>

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:30.220
<i>The stage you're all dancing on</i>

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:29.880
Explode!

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:32.510
<i>is mine.</i>

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:35.820
<i>Your heart is my puppet,</i>

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:35.100
So fun!

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.340
Mobius is the best!

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:39.240
<i>so you can do as you please,</i>

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:38.830
Thank you, μ!

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:41.930
Damn that mad woman!

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:42.570
<i>but let me have some fun,</i>

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:43.230
Marie-chan,

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:46.250
<i>with your insuppressible desires!</i>

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:46.250
if you have dreams, 
let's realize them in reality.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:49.370
<i>If the dream will never end,</i>

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:48.410
Even if you stay here in Mobius forever...

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:51.550
Huh?! What are you spouting?!

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:52.750
<i>then let's just destroy it all!</i>

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:56.220
This moment right now 
is my greatest happiness!

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:57.800
<i>I don't need this worthless world.</i>

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:59.300
That's your happiness, right, Wicked!

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:02.490
<i>That's my dream!</i>

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:01.920
But this Go-Home Club?

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:03.400
Are you all stupid?!

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:06.310
If you don't like Mobius, then die here!

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:11.440
<i>Come on, show me that thing you all have,</i>

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:09.110
Whoops!

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:15.490
I'll be sure to kill you later, 
so just hold tight for a while.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:14.300
<i>those beautiful bonds!</i>

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:17.450
<i>I'll teach you just how</i>

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.080
<i>nauseatingly worthless they are!</i>

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.560
<i>Now, you'll dance as I command you,</i>

00:09:20.270 --> 00:09:21.740
Hey, Thorn!

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.120
Don't get in my way!

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.070
I told you, didn't I?

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:26.640
<i>with the palm of my hand!</i>

00:09:25.070 --> 00:09:27.580
Don't lay a hand on Satake Shogo.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:29.770
<i>Everyone will find their hearts entranced</i>

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:32.140
<i>by this ultimate stage.</i>

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:31.960
Whatever.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:35.920
There's still plenty of other toys here.

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:39.010
I'll play with you all until you break.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:44.630
Shikishima... Ritsu...

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.570
Th-The program...

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:47.230
Huh?

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:49.640
M-Mine's not enough...

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:54.440
I'm blocked from accessing
 the s-system program.

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.480
What are you talking about?

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:58.700
More importantly, how are you here?!

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:02.790
G-Give me admin... p-privileges.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:03.910
H-Hurry...

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:06.160
Can you hear me, Shikishima?

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.830
There hasn't been a single case of an
 Astral Syndrome patient recovering.

00:10:10.220 --> 00:10:12.040
So how are you...

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:17.300
Hurry. I-I need a-administrator privileges.

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:20.750
Listen, answer my question!

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:22.200
How are you here?

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.760
How did you get in here?!

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.020
<b>System Development Team
Tachibana Shingo</b>

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.730
You were the one following me, weren't you?

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:31.980
I thought it was that persistent press again.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.780
I-I really need them.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:39.950
I have to do this, for everyone's sake.

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:47.160
The company's been in big trouble
 ever since you fell asleep.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:52.060
The public's been railing at us,
 and our close team disbanded.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:56.630
As you can see, everyone's left me now.

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:00.090
A-Activate it.

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:02.000
Come on, listen!

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:02.740
Hurry...

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:12.630
Ichika...

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:19.360
Shogo, are you pointing a gun at me?

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:27.490
Is that what you wanted?

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:29.990
H-Hey!

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:38.680
It's about time, isn't it?

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:43.420
If you talk to me, then I'll do 
anything I can do to help you.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:50.420
I'm fully aware that you're
 an incredible programmer,

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:54.730
but that doesn't mean you need
 to take it all on yourself, right?

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.690
You have difficulty interacting with others?

00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:03.550
Why don't you start out
 by casually approaching them?

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:06.740
Once you do, I think 
you'll find a new perspective.

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:08.910
As I've told you before,

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:13.040
you should give yourself a bit more credit.

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:19.130
You're always comparing yourself to others,

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:22.380
but everyone has their own issues.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:25.970
There isn't a single person in this world
 who doesn't carry some worry or problem.

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:31.560
<i>It's my fault μ...</i>

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:34.900
<i>She just wants to make everyone happy.</i>

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:36.730
I have to restore her.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:39.360
I have to patch her.

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:42.360
Back to the kind μ she was.

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:48.020
You look distraught, but it's better
 if you don't take it all on yourself.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:51.910
Rely on me. We were on
 the same team, right?

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.680
It was a constant streak of all-nighters,

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.290
but even that was fun.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:00.840
We were all partners in
 developing μ together, weren't we?

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:03.720
Y-You always did that.

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:08.720
Hey, you come, too!

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:17.930
Forget about him.

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:19.610
He seems to prefer being alone, anyway.

00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:23.070
You're right. Sorry.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:30.330
You always paid attention to me,

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:31.990
because I was lonely.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.460
That made me miserable.

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:39.130
You tiptoed around me.

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:41.960
I was always a social outcast,

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:45.520
and you w-were always in the spotlight.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:48.620
You were so bright that
 it felt like you were rubbing it in.

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:50.140
Shikishima...

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:01.860
Too bad!

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:05.160
I've been wanting to play with you,

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:07.740
so I've rigged up fireworks
 throughout the school!

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:10.150
Let's have even more fun together!

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:14.490
That's the spirit, Traitor-kun!

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:17.910
You betrayed us too, Marie-sempai!

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:21.590
Bye-bye!

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:27.800
Kensuke-kun...

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:31.470
This is too good!

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:35.800
Here in this world, I can run
 wild as much as I want!

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:38.280
I can move my arms and legs freely!

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:41.370
I can break whatever I want!

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:43.630
The more the better!

00:14:43.630 --> 00:14:47.070
The only time I feel alive is

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:49.860
when I'm crushing little critters like you all!

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:54.120
Now, time to enjoy this!

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:03.790
Man, hot-blooded developments
 really aren't my style.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:05.210
Kensuke-kun.

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:07.710
Hey, is that...

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:11.260
Oh, looks like I'm able to do it, too.

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:16.340
You really are shallow.

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:18.480
I get that a lot.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:21.450
Hey, don't ruin the party.

00:15:21.450 --> 00:15:24.230
I still haven't had enough fun yet.

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:26.280
My apologies,

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:30.400
but we're already worn out 
and near our limits.

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:33.910
So I'm going to use those fireworks there.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.150
If I recall,

00:15:35.150 --> 00:15:39.540
you set some explosives up 
right beneath your feet, Sempai.

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:51.040
Not enough!

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:53.910
I can still keep going and going!

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:57.950
Let's enjoy this world more and more!

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:00.200
Marie-chan—

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:01.690
Don't pity me!

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:03.670
I'll kill you!

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.020
I'll kill you for sure!

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.250
Morita, let's go. It's dangerous.

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:17.640
Have you ever experienced it?!

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:22.660
Having your family wish for your death!

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:25.880
Have you?!

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:34.790
Ichika, I'm sorry.

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:38.710
There's nothing I can ever
 do to pay for my sin.

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:41.430
I understand why you would hate me.

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:46.400
I can understand that your happiness
 is to see me suffer as well.

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:48.040
But how did you...

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:51.580
How did a dead person manage
 to come here to Mobius?

00:16:52.130 --> 00:16:53.930
I can't understand that.

00:16:54.610 --> 00:16:55.360
But...

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:58.830
But let's end this already.

00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:01.770
Be quiet! Ichika still exists!

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:07.000
Ichika lives on here, here in Mobius!

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:11.820
Who... are you?

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:17.870
If they don't they stop the Rogues soon,

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:20.990
then both μ and Mobius
 will steadily get crazier.

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:24.850
Huh? Justice always saves
 the world from a crisis!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:26.230
Let's go, everyone!

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.310
You're annoying, so stop taking charge.

00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:36.000
I hated this world.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:39.200
The commuter trains, everyone at work,

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:44.200
the counseling room full of plants,
 greasy smelling ramen,

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:46.660
as well as you and your kindness.

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:52.510
Though, what I hated most of all

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:56.420
was myself, and my inability to fit into reality.

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:58.890
μ was all I had.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.060
She was my only...

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:05.040
I'm happy.

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:08.120
Since you're listening to me talk.

00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:09.730
What's happiness?

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:13.230
It's hard to define.

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:17.740
For instance? When do people feel happiness?

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.660
Well...

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:23.450
Normally, they feel happiness

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:25.620
when they eat good food.

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:28.080
So is good food happiness?

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:29.420
Yeah...

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:33.250
Also, having a pretty, cute girlfriend...

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:35.210
Pretty and cute?

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:38.700
A-Also, when realizing oneself...

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:42.180
When you're able to become
 who you want to be.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:45.390
You don't want pain or suffering?

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:48.980
No, it's better without those.

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:53.940
<i>I want to know more and more
 about happiness, Ritsu!</i>

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:59.370
Then, she left.

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:03.920
To change people's suffering
 and sadness into happiness.

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:05.460
She left me.

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:08.370
<b>Breaking News</b>

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:08.370
<b>New Patient, 17th this Month
Doctors Hurry to Analyze the Cause of this 
Mysterious, Modern Disease</b>

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:10.160
When everyone was being taken away one after another, I thought...

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:11.630
"Next will be me."

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:13.960
"My turn is next."

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:18.030
But no matter how long I waited,

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:20.930
μ wouldn't take me into Mobius.

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:22.830
Mobius?

00:19:22.830 --> 00:19:26.890
So I went to Mobius myself.

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:30.940
I bid farewell to my most hated self,

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:35.670
cast aside my memories of being me, and became who I wanted to be.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:40.100
I became you—someone well-adjusted and well-liked by everyone.

00:19:42.390 --> 00:19:46.010
So I could meet her again.

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:50.620
But, I realized something.

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:55.460
What μ was creating was fake happiness.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:59.090
I can't let μ keep doing that.

00:19:59.440 --> 00:20:00.650
So...

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:02.800
I'm going to restore μ!

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:04.120
Restore?

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:05.430
You mean...

00:20:06.150 --> 00:20:07.930
Have you figured it out?!

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.930
What's causing that disease?!

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:12.390
It has to be something in μ's program, right?

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:15.310
Then there has to be something I can do, too!

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:17.820
Let's work together and patch her!

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:19.280
Together we'll patch μ's program!

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:20.240
I will!

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:24.460
I have to do this!

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:27.550
If I don't, then I won't be able to change.

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:30.160
I'll never be able to change.

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:33.750
I have to save them!
 μ and everyone else!

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:39.960
I'll go make some coffee.

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:43.930
You've changed, Shikishima.

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:46.730
Where is it?

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:48.930
This part's functioning normally,

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:50.510
so is it the code?

00:20:50.510 --> 00:20:52.800
Argh, dammit! What's different?!

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:54.440
What is causing this abnormality?

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:56.240
What do I do?

00:20:56.240 --> 00:20:59.820
How can I hear your voice again?

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:01.780
Answer me, μ!

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:06.950
I need to patch μ.

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:10.080
She's singing about 
that happiness so gleefully.

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:12.330
I have to stop her.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:13.410
I do.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:14.580
I do.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:15.420
I do.

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:19.290
Because I made her!

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:24.260
<i>I finally managed to hear your real voice.</i>

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:27.590
<i>It was hard, wasn't it?</i>

00:21:27.990 --> 00:21:29.400
<i>It hurt, didn't it?</i>

00:21:29.860 --> 00:21:33.910
<i>Those dark, muddy feelings have reached me.</i>

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:36.520
<i>So you should tell her directly.</i>

00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:39.670
<i>Let's go back, to Mobius.</i>

00:23:11.490 --> 00:23:14.560
You can be happy in Mobius.

00:23:14.560 --> 00:23:17.910
Everyone should be in here.

00:23:17.910 --> 00:23:23.790
Forever, forever inside me.

00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:26.470
Right, Ritsu?

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:29.880
And suddenly, a giant UMA, 
Devil Mammo, appears!

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:41.020
<b>Episode 12: Destroy your ideals and
 self, and return to hell and reality.</b>

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:33.930
Can the President really capture 
Devil Mammo and return to reality?!

00:23:33.930 --> 00:23:37.220
Final Episode: Destroy your ideals and
 self, and return to hell and reality.

00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:40.540
To the hopeful future! Ready, go!
